Ajoy Tools License Agreement

Effective 17 October 2026

1. The agreement

This agreement is between AJOY and the person or organisation licensed to use Ajoy Tools. It covers the installer, Maya tools, scripts, interface assets, documentation, updates and related licensing services provided under the Ajoy Tools name.
By installing or using the software, you agree to these terms. If you act for an organisation, you must have authority to accept them. If you do not agree, do not install or use the software. A purchase confirmation may specify your plan, licensed computer count and subscription period.

2. What your license allows

During your active, paid subscription, AJOY grants you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to install and use Ajoy Tools in Autodesk Maya for your own or your organisation’s production work, including commercial projects, on the number of computers covered by your subscription.
One license covers one computer. A studio code may cover multiple computers up to the purchased count.
Your production output remains yours or the relevant rights holder’s. This agreement does not give AJOY ownership of your scenes, animation, renders or exports.
Keep your code private. Use it only for the named subscriber’s licensed computers. Contact support before moving or replacing licensed machines.
Ajoy Tools itself remains AJOY’s property. Buying access grants permission to use it; it does not transfer ownership of its code, branding or protected assets.

3. Online and Offline access

Online
Requires internet access when Maya starts to check the subscription. Updates are installed automatically.

Offline
Requires internet to install, then works without a continuing connection. You choose when to check for updates.

Both plans include all 13 tools for Autodesk Maya 2023 and newer on Windows. Offline access is still a subscription: working without internet does not extend the paid license period.

4. Subscriptions, savings and cancellation

Subscriptions are priced per computer and billed monthly or yearly as shown before purchase. Yearly billing is 20% less than twelve monthly payments for the same plan and country. It is paid annually; a monthly equivalent is a comparison, not a monthly payment option. Applicable taxes are additional and must be shown before payment.
Returning subscriber rewards are applied automatically after email ownership and paid history are verified: 5% off the second monthly payment, 5% off the third monthly payment, and no monthly loyalty discount after that. The second annual payment (first yearly renewal) receives an additional 10% off the price after the standard 20% yearly saving, once; later annual payments keep the standard yearly saving only. That yearly loyalty reward is an express exception to the usual minimum price. Each reward is available once per verified customer, not once per computer. We count confirmed full paid billing periods, excluding failed, refunded, disputed and prorated charges; repeated invoices for the same period do not advance a reward. A consumed reward is not reissued after a refund. Loyalty rewards and coupons do not stack; the better eligible offer is used.

Coupons apply only when validated and eligible for your selected plan, billing period, country and quantity. A coupon may not combine with yearly savings or another discount. The confirmed order total governs a purchase.
Online payments are not open yet.
The preview billing page cannot charge you or create a subscription. Payment-provider details, renewal terms and any purchase-specific refund policy must be shown before a payment can be accepted.

For an active subscription, you may stop future renewals using the cancellation option supplied with your purchase or by contacting support. Unless the purchase terms or law provide otherwise, cancellation takes effect at the end of the paid period. Refund and consumer rights required by law remain available. A price change must be disclosed before it applies to a renewal.

5. Protect the toolkit and your access

You must not, or help another person to:
Crack, patch, emulate or bypass activation, expiry, computer limits or other license protections.
Share, publish, sell or use access codes outside the subscriber’s licensed computers.
Copy, host, resell, rent, sublicense or distribute the protected tool package or its code and assets without permission. The original setup file alone may be shared freely, with its notices intact.
Reverse engineer, decompile, decrypt or extract protected software, except to the extent applicable law permits despite this restriction.
Copy protected code, artwork or documentation into another product, or create derivative works from those protected materials without permission. This does not restrict independently created work or rights that the law reserves to you.
Tamper with service requests, guess access codes, interfere with servers, remove ownership notices or use the toolkit after your permission ends.

6. Updates, support and safe use

An active subscription includes help with installation, updates and bug fixes by email. Offline subscribers receive priority support. No particular response time or custom pipeline integration is promised unless separately agreed.
Features and compatibility may evolve. Keep backups and test tools on copies of important scenes. Export tools can overwrite output files when you choose that option. Some features require Maya plug-ins, FFmpeg, available codecs or a compatible rig, as described in the user guide.

7. License checks and privacy

Activation uses your access code, a stable device identifier, computer name, Windows user name, local network address, Maya version and Python build identifier to issue the appropriate package and administer computer limits. The installer’s activation request does not upload your scenes or project files.
The privacy notice explains website requests, activation records, billing details, verification providers, retention and how to exercise applicable privacy rights.

8. When permission ends

Your permission to use Ajoy Tools ends when your paid subscription expires or the agreement is terminated. Stop using the tools and remove installed copies when that happens, including Offline installations.
We may suspend or terminate access for a material breach, such as code sharing, circumvention or unauthorised distribution. Where appropriate and legally required, we will explain the issue and give a reasonable opportunity to resolve it. Contact support if you believe access was restricted in error.
Copyright and other legal remedies may be available for infringement or unlawful access, subject to applicable law. These terms do not predetermine a court’s findings or remove mandatory refund, notice or consumer rights. Ownership, restrictions, accrued payment obligations and applicable liability provisions continue as relevant after termination.

9. Reliability and warranty

Ajoy Tools is provided “as is” and “as available” to the extent permitted by law. We aim to make it reliable, but do not promise uninterrupted service, error-free operation or suitability for every rig and pipeline. Statutory warranties and rights that cannot lawfully be excluded are preserved.

10. Limits of liability

To the fullest extent permitted by law, AJOY is not liable for indirect or consequential losses, including lost profits, lost production time or lost data, arising from use of or inability to use the toolkit. AJOY’s total liability for a claim is limited to subscription fees you paid in the twelve months before the event giving rise to it.
These limits do not exclude or restrict liability that the law does not allow us to limit, including mandatory consumer protections.

11. Applicable law and changes

These terms are governed by the laws of India, subject to any mandatory rights and protections available where you live. Competent courts in India may hear disputes, without limiting jurisdiction or remedies that applicable law requires elsewhere.
We may revise these terms and publish an updated date. Material changes will be notified where required. A change does not remove rights already accrued or override the terms of a completed purchase where applicable law protects them.

